    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Reorder HTML module and update letter challenge]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40845</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40845"/>
        <updated>2025-08-22T16:03:11.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR is part of a series in which I update the Learn area "Challenge" articles. In general, they need to be modernized, restructured, and put in better positions in the modules so they are spaced out better and test subjects that have already been covered.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR improves the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Marking_up_a_letter" rel="nofollow">Marking up a letter challenge</a>. Specifically, it:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Places it just after the "Advanced text" article and skilltest, to limit the scope of what is being tested a bit.</li>
<li>Puts the "Structuring documents" article after that skilltest.</li>
<li>Removes the hyperlink test from the challenge, as it won't have been covered yet.</li>
<li>Modernizes the look of the example, streamlines the question wording, and presents the sample text to work on and finished example as live samples.</li>
<li>Relies on the user using MDN Playground to solve the challenge, not their local environment.</li>
<li>Includes a summary/detail containing the final markup, to allow the reader to self-assess more easily.</li>
</ul>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



]]></content>
